# Response headers for the static assets served by Cloudflare (dist/).
#
# Cloudflare's asset layer applies this file to every static-asset response,
# including the app shell the Worker returns for /app. It is configuration,
# not content: Cloudflare does not publish it as a file.
#
# Responses generated by the Worker itself (everything under /api, and the
# 404/405 answers for paths that match no file) get the equivalent headers
# from cloudflare/platform.js. tests/platform/cloudflare-config.test.mjs keeps
# the two sets in step.
#
# The resource policy (script-src, connect-src, frame-src, ...) stays in the
# <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"> tag of index.html so that the
# same policy also protects the PC-local build. The header below adds the
# directives a <meta> tag cannot express (frame-ancestors) or does not carry
# (form-action). Browsers enforce both policies together.
#
# X-Robots-Tag keeps this STAGING deployment out of search indexes.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
